      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T10:20:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can\u0027t do the same thing with setRequireCompatChange* though. The point of these methods is to not send to apps that declare the receiver in their manifest, but send it to apps that register dynamically. This was done for performance purposes, to avoid spinning up apps with broadcasts like CONNECTIVITY_ACTION which can be frequent.\n\nI think there is still a use case for this.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "83f993d26b4f67b113eb8abb478812bb9d88067e",
